<%# Wippli: two logos, the mail client shows one. Light (purple wordmark) by default; the negative (white wordmark,
    orange SIGN unchanged) when the reader is in dark mode: Apple Mail / iOS / Gmail via prefers-color-scheme in the
    layout's style block, Outlook via its [data-ogsc] hook. Clients that understand neither keep the light logo. %>
<p>
  <img src="<%= Docuseal::DEFAULT_APP_URL %>/wippli-sign-logo-email.png"
       width="160" height="28" alt="<%= Docuseal.product_name %>" class="wippli-logo-light"
       style="display:block;border:0;outline:none;text-decoration:none;max-width:100%;height:auto;">
  <!--[if !mso]><! -->
  <img src="<%= Docuseal::DEFAULT_APP_URL %>/wippli-sign-logo-email-dark.png"
       width="160" height="28" alt="<%= Docuseal.product_name %>" class="wippli-logo-dark"
       style="display:none;border:0;outline:none;text-decoration:none;max-width:100%;height:auto;mso-hide:all;">
  <!--<![endif]-->
</p>
